My third Slash'em ascension.  A necromancer after a monk and a valkyrie. 
I guess, doppelganger necromancers have to be counted as easy, since the 
doppelganger abilities give you a lot of choices in early game. 
Nevertheless, necromancers start with so weak stats that I have not 
managed to get one going that did not have either the magic missile 
spell or the force bolt spell in their initial inventory.  The other two 
possibilities, wizard lock and knock, are not useful for early survival. 
  The drain level spell that is guaranteed for necromencers as starting 
knowledge is not too useful, as initially you cannot cast it often -- it 
is a third-level spell -- and later the monsters don't die on being hit 
by it once, since most of them are higher than level 1.

Besides the fact that necromancers don't exist in vanilla, one reason 
for me to try that class was their intrinsic sickness resistance and 
level-drain resistance, which are not helping much to survive in the 
early game but made wands of draining harmless and the encounters with 
Demogorgon and Pestilence a breeze.  The ability to detect the buc 
status of objects immediately is extremely useful, of course.

Anyway, most of my ascensions are pretty ordinary, so I will refrain 
from telling a long story here (most of the time I get almost no 
comments) and just append my log-file here which should give the general 
picture.  I *think* that my character started out as a male but became 
female when a polymorph did not succeed and resulted in "a new 
doppelganger" instead.  It was the first time I messed around with a 
gypsy and when she gave me a wish, I thought I might as well burn it by 
wishing for the Bat from Hell.  I did not expect to get it as there were 
already seven artifacts in the game.  But I got it -- this was after 
having killed Demogorgon -- and the game started to rock.  However, I 
found that Serpent's Tongue, the garanteed first gift for necromancers 
(I got it differently, though) is not to be sneezed at either.  Damages 
of about 20 per hit to all monsters when enchanted to +7, bigger damage 
and occasional insta-kills for non-poison resistant monsters are not 
that bad.

